        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicmissouri.org/items/show/152",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits just north of the confluence of Hurricane Creek and Crooked Creek, giving it a unique riverside setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble_Hill%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Marble Hill’s public library, the Bollinger County Library, serves as a community hub for history and learning.",
